 Step-by-Step JVM Tuning Process :-
 Step 1

 Collect metrics
 CPU | Memory | Heap | GC | Threads | Class Loading

 Step 2
 Enable GC Logging

 Java 17

 -Xlog:gc*:gc.log

 Look for
 Young GC | Full GC | Pause Time  | Allocation Rate

 Step 3
 Analyze Heap | jmap | Heap Dump | MAT

 Find

 Largest objects | Memory leak | Duplicate objects
 Step 4

 Thread Dump | jstack

  Check
 Deadlock | Waiting threads |  Blocked threads

 Step 5

 Tune JVM Parameters

 Heap Size

 Initial Heap = -Xms4g

 Maximum Heap = -Xmx4g

 Recommendation

 Keep

 Xms = Xmx

 to avoid heap resizing.

 Garbage Collector

 Default (Java 17)

 G1GC

 Enable

 -XX:+UseG1GC
 Pause Time Goal
 -XX:MaxGCPauseMillis=200

 G1GC tries to keep pause under 200 ms.

 Heap Occupancy
 -XX:InitiatingHeapOccupancyPercent=45

 Starts concurrent marking earlier.

 String Deduplication

 Useful if many duplicate Strings.

 -XX:+UseStringDeduplication
 GC Threads
 -XX:ParallelGCThreads=8
 -XX:ConcGCThreads=4

 Tune according to CPU cores.

 Metaspace

 Instead of PermGen

 -XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=512m
 Direct Memory

 For Netty

 -XX:MaxDirectMemorySize=2g
 Container Awareness

 Docker

 -XX:+UseContainerSupport

 Java 17 enables this by default.

 Example JVM Options
 -Xms8g
 -Xmx8g

 -XX:+UseG1GC

 -XX:MaxGCPauseMillis=200

 -XX:+UseStringDeduplication

 -XX:InitiatingHeapOccupancyPercent=45

 -Xlog:gc*:gc.log
 Common Scenarios
 Scenario 1

 Problem

 Young GC every second

 Solution

 Increase Eden Space  | Increase Heap | Reduce object creation

 Scenario 2

 Problem

 Full GC every minute

 Solution

 Increase Heap | Find memory leak | Analyze Heap Dump

 Scenario 3

 Problem

 API freezes for 20 seconds

 Reason

 Long Full GC

 Solution

 G1GC
 More Heap
 Reduce old generation usage
 Scenario 4

 Problem

 OutOfMemoryError

 Solution

 Heap Dump
 MAT Analysis
 Fix leak instead of only increasing heap
